first fires then floods  hopes are dwindling in this town that  missing loved ones will still be alive  those who survived the floods in  buzzkirt on the black sea wait anxiously  for news  with a population of fewer than nine  thousand most people will know someone  affected by this tragedy  for elias the devastation is difficult  to comprehend  my aunt is missing her husband is  missing her twin grandchildren are  missing the wife of our building manager  is missing along with their two children  his relative and local business owner  turon describes the moment flood waters  rushed in at the very moment they were  paying tribute to his uncle at his  funeral  people were shouting and screaming  asking others to run away we looked and  saw the flood waters coming our way from  the direction of the post office we fled  up hill running past the bridge to bring  ourselves to safety  the flood described as one of turkey's  worst was the second natural disaster to  strike the country this month  chaos in the north just as authorities  had declared wildfires in the south had  been brought under control  on friday president erdogan visited the  region declaring three disaster zones  he promised to defer taxes and offered  relief for all those affected  the nation's disaster agency has  deployed nearly six thousand personnel  to the hardest hit areas  almost half a meter of rain has fallen  in less than three days causing rivers  to overflow  torrents of water have been tossing cars  filling streets with debris and wiping  entire houses from their foundations  more than 2 000 people have been  evacuated from their homes many with the  help of helicopters and boats  some having fled to their rooftops as a  last resort  hundreds of villages are without  electricity and people say they can't  reach their loved ones by phone  volunteers are doing what they can to  deliver aid as rescue teams continue to  try to save more lives  in this town where buildings line the  waterfront 